    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp35Tests` soft-match checkpoint.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") rule for owner creation.\n\n**Behavior:** When a new owner is not a hard duplicate (identity-key collision \u2192 still 409) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) and `postcode` while carrying a *different* normalized telephone, the owner is still created and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (lowest id when several match, for determinism). Otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false` and the `possibleDuplicateOf` field is absent.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added read-only `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the two persisted fields (`possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of` columns) with getters/setters.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 after the identity-collision check, a new `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` helper detects the soft match and sets the flag/id (or `false`).\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the two new `owners` columns (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the same-named fields into the DTO, and the values persist so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads them back \u2014 no mapper changes were needed.",
